    "note": "Sweeps the lot-relative |z| safety-net gate (2\u03c3\u20137\u03c3). This isolates ONLY the raw |z| gate in isolation for analytical insight. Key finding: at low \u03c3 the gate is noisy (nominal FP rises), and at high \u03c3 (e.g. 7\u03c3) it MISSES borderline latent creep just above the 3\u03c3 dynamic gate (11.5\u201314\u00b5A) while still catching extreme defects (30\u201348\u00b5A). This is why the production system is a CASCADE - IF + criticality gate carry the sub-outlier screening, and the 7\u03c3 z-net is purely a belt-and-suspenders catastrophic backstop. The full pipeline (A+C+B) achieves the 100% recall reported in Phase 1, and this table explains why no single |z| threshold could do that alone."
